/T (For the purposes of this paper, the authors focus on the financial component of ROI, with social impact and other non-financial benefits addressed separately under Level 3 metrics. This approach ensures a precise, quantifiable foundation for decision making while recognising that the broader value of AI deployments will be captured elsewhere. The authors took inspiration from a recent model focusing on the creation of a Value Score as Nominator and a Cost score as Denominator [12] to implement this approach.)
/E (For the purposes of this paper, the authors focus on the financial component of ROI, with social impact and other non-financial benefits addressed separately under Level 3 metrics. This approach ensures a precise, quantifiable foundation for decision making while recognising that the broader value of AI deployments will be captured elsewhere. The authors took inspiration from a recent model focusing on the creation of a Value Score as Nominator and a Cost score as Denominator [12] to implement this approach.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
